  "result": "If I could change the world in one way, I\u2019d give every person the ability to truly feel what someone else is feeling\u2014joy, fear, grief or hope\u2014at the moment it\u2019s experienced. No translators or explanations needed: a direct, momentary empathic connection between any two minds.\n\nImagine:\n\u2022 A politician experiencing the hunger and fear of a refugee makes different laws.  \n\u2022 A polluter feeling, first\u2010hand, the ache of dying forests stops digging for profit.  \n\u2022 A teenager understanding a bully\u2019s own pain chooses kindness instead.  \n\u2022 Strangers in conflict realize they share the same hopes and vulnerabilities.\n\nThat single shift\u2014universal, instantaneous empathy\u2014would dissolve most barriers: national, cultural, ideological. We wouldn\u2019t need endless debates to grasp \u201cthe other side.\u201d Compassion would be baked into every choice. Conflicts rooted in misunderstanding would wither. Cooperation, resource\u2010sharing and creative problem-solving would skyrocket.\n\nIn that world, \u201cus versus them\u201d becomes impossible. We become \u201cwe.\u201d And suddenly, tackling climate change, eradicating poverty or ending war feels less like heroic struggles and more like natural outgrowths of a collective heart.",
